# Trust a reverse proxy's X-Forwarded-For header. **Not loaded:** copy this
# file to a name ending in .conf in this directory, or mount your own there,
# for example
#
#   -v ./trusted-proxies.conf:/usr/local/apache2/conf/trusted-proxies.d/trusted-proxies.conf:ro
#
# By default this image trusts no proxy, and REMOTE_ADDR and the access log
# show the address that connected.
#
# List only your proxy's own address or subnet. Apache replaces the client
# address with the value of the header when, and only when, the request comes
# from an address listed here. Anything else that can reach Apache from a listed
# address can set the header to any value, so a wide range such as 172.16.0.0/12
# trusts every container on every Docker network, not just the proxy.
#
# Keep both directives. RemoteIPHeader on its own, with no RemoteIPTrustedProxy
# or RemoteIPInternalProxy, believes the header from every client.

RemoteIPHeader X-Forwarded-For
RemoteIPTrustedProxy 172.18.0.2
